{"id":"h1-03-c2","title":"Availability, nines, SLI/SLO/error budgets","scopeHtml":"<p>Scope: nines, series and parallel availability, SLI SLO SLA, error budgets and burn rate. Questions are still to be written.</p>","notes":[{"id":"what-availability-means","title":"What availability means","html":"<p><strong>Availability is the fraction of time (or requests) in which the service works correctly.</strong> Availability = uptime / (uptime + downtime). It is usually quoted in \"nines\".</p>\n<p>It is not the same as durability (data is not lost) or reliability in general. S3 is designed for 99.99% availability but 99.999999999% (11 nines) durability: it may be briefly unreachable but should never lose your object.</p>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 455.2 68\" width=\"455.2\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Available means the request succeeds within expectations\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M102 34 L158 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 34 L158 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M248 34 L304 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M248 34 L304 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Client</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"203\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Service</text><rect x=\"304\" y=\"12\" width=\"139.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"373.6\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Correct response</text></svg><figcaption>Available means the request succeeds within expectations</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Worked example.</strong> 30-day month = 43,200 minutes. 99.9% availability allows 43.2 minutes of downtime; 99.99% allows 4.3 minutes.</p>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> AWS publishes SLAs per service (for example EC2 region-level 99.99%, S3 Standard 99.9%; confirm current SLA pages). Stripe and Google Cloud also publish status and post-mortems.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> A shop's opening hours: \"open 99.9% of the hours it promised\".</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Confusing availability with durability.</li>\n<li>Measuring only server uptime: a server that answers 500s is \"up\" but not available. Count successful requests.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"the-nines-table","title":"The nines table","html":"<p><strong>Memorise this table.</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span>Availability  Downtime/year   Downtime/month   Typical meaning</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>99%           3.65 days       7.2 hours        hobby / batch</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>99.9%         8.76 hours      43.8 minutes     standard web service</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>99.95%        4.4 hours       21.9 minutes     managed DB tier</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>99.99%        52.6 minutes    4.4 minutes      multi-AZ, automated failover</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>99.999%       5.26 minutes    26 seconds       multi-region, extreme cost</span></span></code></pre>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 552 68\" width=\"552\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Each nine is roughly 10x cheaper to ignore and 10x harder to hit\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M102 34 L158 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 34 L158 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;0.251;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M248 34 L304 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M248 34 L304 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M394 34 L450 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M394 34 L450 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;0.751;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">99%</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"203\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">99.9%</text><rect x=\"304\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"349\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">99.99%</text><rect x=\"450\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"495\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">99.999%</text></svg><figcaption>Each nine is roughly 10x cheaper to ignore and 10x harder to hit</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Decision gravity.</strong> The availability target drives architecture: 99.9% can be one region with multi-AZ (reversible, modest cost); 99.99% needs automated failover and careful deploys; 99.999% needs active-active multi-region, which is a one-way door in complexity, data consistency, and cost. Do not promise more than the business pays for. Also your target cannot exceed your dependencies' (next section).</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> Delivery promises: \"within a week\" is cheap, \"within 10 minutes\" needs a dark store next door.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Promising five nines for a normal CRUD app.</li>\n<li>Forgetting planned maintenance counts unless excluded in the SLA.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"availability-in-series-and-in-parallel","title":"Availability in series and in parallel","html":"<p><strong>Series (all needed): multiply. Parallel (any one is enough): combine failure probabilities.</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span>Series:   A = A1 x A2 x A3</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>Parallel: A = 1 - (1 - A1) x (1 - A2)</span></span></code></pre>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 579.6 68\" width=\"579.6\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Series: every hop must work\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M102 34 L158 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 34 L158 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;0.251;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M275.6 34 L331.6 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M275.6 34 L331.6 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M421.6 34 L477.6 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M421.6 34 L477.6 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;0.751;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Client</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"12\" width=\"117.60000000000001\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"216.8\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Load balancer</text><rect x=\"331.6\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"376.6\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">App</text><rect x=\"477.6\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"22\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"522.6\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Database</text></svg><figcaption>Series: every hop must work</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Worked example (series).</strong> LB 99.99%, app 99.95%, DB 99.95%, cache 99.9%: 0.9999 x 0.9995 x 0.9995 x 0.999 = 99.79%, about 18.5 hours of downtime a year, worse than any single part.</p>\n<p><strong>Worked example (parallel).</strong> Two app instances each 99% available and independent: 1 - 0.01 x 0.01 = 99.99%. Caveat: failures are rarely independent (same deploy, same bug, same AZ), so real gains are lower. Redundancy must be across failure domains (instances, racks, AZs, regions).</p>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 433.6 130\" width=\"433.6\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Parallel: either server is enough\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M102 65 L158 65\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 65 L158 65\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M275.6 65 L331.6 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M275.6 65 L331.6 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M275.6 65 L331.6 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M275.6 65 L331.6 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"43\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Client</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"43\" width=\"117.60000000000001\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"216.8\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Load balancer</text><rect x=\"331.6\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"376.6\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">App 1</text><rect x=\"331.6\" y=\"74\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"376.6\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">App 2</text></svg><figcaption>Parallel: either server is enough</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> AWS places instances across 3 AZs; losing one AZ should keep the service up. Google and Netflix design for region failure for tier-1 services (Netflix regularly evacuates a region).</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> A chain of links is as weak as the weakest; two ropes holding the same weight are safer than one.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Computing parallel availability as if failures were independent when they share a deploy or a database.</li>\n<li>Adding a redundant app tier but leaving a single database.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"sli-slo-sla","title":"SLI, SLO, SLA","html":"<p><strong>SLI is what you measure. SLO is the target you set. SLA is the contract with penalties.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>SLI (indicator):</strong> a ratio, such as good requests / total requests, or fraction of requests under 300 ms.</li>\n<li><strong>SLO (objective):</strong> internal target, such as 99.9% of requests succeed over 30 days.</li>\n<li><strong>SLA (agreement):</strong> external promise with refunds, usually looser than the SLO (SLA 99.9%, SLO 99.95%).</li>\n</ul>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 553.6 68\" width=\"553.6\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"From measurement to contract\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M129.60000000000002 34 L185.60000000000002 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M129.60000000000002 34 L185.60000000000002 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M296 34 L352 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M296 34 L352 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"12\" width=\"117.60000000000001\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"70.80000000000001\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">SLI (measure)</text><rect x=\"185.60000000000002\" y=\"12\" width=\"110.4\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"240.8\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">SLO (target)</text><rect x=\"352\" y=\"12\" width=\"189.6\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"446.8\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">SLA (promise + penalty)</text></svg><figcaption>From measurement to contract</figcaption></figure>\n<p>Good SLIs: availability (non-5xx / total), latency (requests &#x3C; 300 ms / total), freshness (data age &#x3C; 1 min), correctness. Measure at the load balancer or from the client side, not from the server's own health.</p>\n<p><strong>Worked example.</strong> SLI: <code>sum(rate(http_requests_total{code!~\"5..\"}[5m])) / sum(rate(http_requests_total[5m]))</code>. SLO: >= 99.9% over rolling 30 days. If the 30-day ratio is 99.95%, you are within target.</p>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\"># Illustrative SLO definition (OpenSLO-style, not exact schema)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#22863A;--shiki-dark:#85E89D\">slo</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">:</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#22863A;--shiki-dark:#85E89D\">  name</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">checkout-availability</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#22863A;--shiki-dark:#85E89D\">  objective</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">99.9</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#22863A;--shiki-dark:#85E89D\">  window</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">30d</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#22863A;--shiki-dark:#85E89D\">  sli</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">good_requests / total_requests</span></span></code></pre>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> Google's SRE book popularised SLI/SLO/error budget. Cloud SLAs give service credits (for example 10% to 100% of the bill) when the SLA is missed.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision gravity.</strong> An SLA is a legal one-way door; tightening it later is hard. Set SLOs conservatively first; they are cheap to adjust.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> SLI is your speedometer, SLO is the speed you aim for, SLA is the fine if you break the limit.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Treating SLO and SLA as the same.</li>\n<li>Picking too many SLIs; start with 2 or 3 (availability, latency).</li>\n<li>Choosing 100% as a target; it is unreachable and blocks all change.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"error-budgets","title":"Error budgets","html":"<p><strong>Error budget = 1 - SLO. It is the amount of unreliability you are allowed, and you can spend it on releases and experiments.</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span>SLO 99.9% over 30 days  -> budget 0.1% -> 43.2 minutes</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>Or in requests: 100M requests/month x 0.001 = 100,000 failed requests allowed</span></span></code></pre>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 408.79999999999995 130\" width=\"408.79999999999995\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Budget decides release speed\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M151.2 34 L207.2 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"1.6s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M151.2 34 L207.2 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"1.6s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M151.2 96 L207.2 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"1.6s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M151.2 96 L207.2 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"1.6s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"12\" width=\"139.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"81.6\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Budget left</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"74\" width=\"139.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"81.6\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Budget exhausted</text><rect x=\"207.2\" y=\"12\" width=\"189.6\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"302\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Ship features</text><rect x=\"207.2\" y=\"74\" width=\"189.6\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"302\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Freeze, fix reliability</text></svg><figcaption>Budget decides release speed</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Burn rate</strong> = how fast the budget is consumed relative to the allowed rate. Burn rate 1 uses the budget exactly at the end of the window; burn rate 14.4 uses a 30-day budget in about 2 days. A common alerting pattern (Google SRE workbook) pages on fast burn over short windows (for example burn 14.4 over 1 h) and tickets on slow burn (burn 1 over 3 days).</p>\n<p><strong>Worked example.</strong> Budget 43.2 min/month. A bad deploy causes 20 min of errors: 46% of budget gone in one day. Policy: pause risky launches until the budget recovers or a postmortem action is done.</p>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> Google SRE teams use budget policies to arbitrate between product velocity and reliability. Many companies track budgets in tools like Prometheus/Grafana, Datadog SLOs or Nobl9.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision gravity.</strong> A budget policy is an organisational choice and reversible, but it only works if leadership honours the freeze.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> A monthly allowance: you can spend on risks until it is gone.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Alerting on raw error spikes instead of burn rate (noisy pages).</li>\n<li>Having an SLO but no consequence when it is breached.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"how-to-reach-higher-availability","title":"How to reach higher availability","html":"<p><strong>Availability comes from removing single points of failure, shrinking the blast radius of changes, and recovering fast.</strong> Two quantities: MTBF (mean time between failures) and MTTR (mean time to repair). Availability = MTBF / (MTBF + MTTR). Cutting MTTR is usually cheaper than raising MTBF.</p>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 459.2 192\" width=\"459.2\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Levers\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M230.4 34 L286.4 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"1.6s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M230.4 34 L286.4 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"1.6s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M230.4 96 L286.4 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"1.6s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M230.4 96 L286.4 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"1.6s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M230.4 158 L286.4 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"1.6s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M230.4 158 L286.4 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"1.6s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"12\" width=\"218.4\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"121.2\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Redundancy</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"74\" width=\"218.4\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"121.2\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Safe deploys</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"136\" width=\"218.4\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"121.2\" y=\"162\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Fast detection and recovery</text><rect x=\"286.4\" y=\"74\" width=\"160.8\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"366.79999999999995\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Higher availability</text></svg><figcaption>Levers</figcaption></figure>\n<p>Checklist:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Redundancy across AZs; stateless tiers behind health-checked LBs.</li>\n<li>Database replication with automated failover (RPO and RTO stated).</li>\n<li>Canary and progressive rollouts, feature flags, instant rollback; most outages follow a change.</li>\n<li>Timeouts, retries with backoff, circuit breakers, load shedding.</li>\n<li>Graceful degradation: serve stale cache or a reduced page rather than an error.</li>\n<li>Runbooks, alerting on SLO burn, regular game days.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Worked example.</strong> Failures once a month (MTBF 720 h) with 60 min to repair: A = 720 / 721 = 99.86%. Cutting repair time to 6 min (auto-failover) gives 99.986%, a 10x gain without making the system fail less.</p>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> Netflix chaos engineering (Chaos Monkey) validates redundancy; Amazon uses cell-based architectures to limit blast radius.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> A hospital: spare generators (redundancy), checklists before surgery (safe change), fast ambulance (low MTTR).</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Focusing only on preventing failure; recovery speed often matters more.</li>\n<li>Forgetting that deployments, not hardware, cause most outages.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"summary","title":"Summary","html":"<ul>\n<li>Availability = successful requests / total (or uptime fraction); durability is different.</li>\n<li>Memorise nines: 99.9% = 8.8 h/year; 99.99% = 53 min/year; 99.999% = 5 min/year.</li>\n<li>Series multiplies (worse); parallel combines (better) if failures are independent.</li>\n<li>SLI = measure, SLO = internal target, SLA = contract with penalty (looser than SLO).</li>\n<li>Error budget = 1 - SLO; spend it on change, freeze when gone; alert on burn rate.</li>\n<li>Raise availability via redundancy, safe deploys and low MTTR; each extra nine costs far more.</li>\n</ul>"}],"questions":[]}